//! license: null) -- the decision-content-only posture: the corpus consumes
//! the DECISION CONTENT with ORIGINAL Rust fixtures below, never source
//! verbatim; any outbound-PR posture for this family is FAIL-CLOSED absent
//! a license (the GPL-3.0 `CVEngine` + undeclared-jeva precedents). 64x64
//! hardware-tile mixed INT8/BF16 weight quantization for decoder linears:
//! a calibrated importance map keeps a small tile fraction (1-20%) in BF16,
//! the rest INT8 with one scale per tile; activations quantize INT8 per
//! 64-COLUMN tile with a batch-wide scale; a row-owned Triton GEMM computes
//! exact INT32 tile dots for INT8 tiles (scaled in FP32, ascending column
//! order) and FP32 tensor-core dots for BF16 tiles, with an in-kernel serial
//! split-K reduction. Weights pack at checkpoint load ("no quantized
//! checkpoint is stored"); a fixed-shape CUDA-graph decoder runs greedy
//! decode.
//!
//! Rules 1-3 (the address-shape law, the batch-wide actmax pass, the
//! direct-launch key completeness). Three count-neutral faces landed on
//! their OWNERS (cite never re-own): the replay-safe self-resetting
//! split-K counter on `splitk-reduce-one-launch-slice-order-pinned`
//! (`gpu_67`), the graph-capture cluster (pool-pinning admission +
//! empty_cache-before-capture + captured-reset independent replay) on
//! `graph-fallback-coverage-ladder` (`gpu_149`), and the sibling-projection
//! act-quant MEMO arm on `fuse-gate-up-gemv-activation` (`gpu_01`) -- see
//! Research 379 + the hosts' `gpu_concept` tails.
//!
